Subject: [PATCH] Keep backward screen-line motion past overlay tails

SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Chen Zhexuan
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

At the end of the accessible buffer a display replacement can consume
an entire candidate row.  With a newline-bearing overlay at that end,
reseating on the preceding buffer line can jump straight back to the
same endpoint.  Counting that line makes a one-line command stall and
larger counts stop short.

Use the raw line boundary for the backward search and its forward
rescan when reseating proves it collapses into the same endpoint.
Preserve the existing wrapped-line correction and iterator state for
ordinary end-of-buffer movement.

--- a/src/xdisp.c
+++ b/src/xdisp.c
@@ -11564,6 +11564,25 @@
       /* Go back -DVPOS buffer lines, but no farther than -DVPOS full
 	 screen lines, and reseat the iterator there.  */
       start_charpos = IT_CHARPOS (*it);
+      if (dvpos < 0 && start_charpos == ZV && start_charpos > BEGV)
+	{
+	  /* An empty display replacement before an end-of-buffer
+	     overlay can make the preceding buffer line reseat at ZV.
+	     Start the backward search at that raw line boundary, so
+	     we don't spend a step landing back at the same position.  */
+	  SAVE_IT (it2, *it, it2data);
+	  back_to_previous_visible_line_start (&it2);
+	  struct text_pos previous = it2.current.pos;
+	  reseat (&it2, previous, true);
+	  bool collapsed = (CHARPOS (previous) < start_charpos
+			    && IT_CHARPOS (it2) == start_charpos);
+	  RESTORE_IT (it, it, it2data);
+	  if (collapsed)
+	    {
+	      reseat_1 (it, previous, true);
+	      start_charpos = CHARPOS (previous);
+	    }
+	}
       if (it->line_wrap == TRUNCATE || nchars_per_row == 0)
 	pos_limit = BEGV;
       else
